This file explains, how to clone the private repo on our EC2:

Option: 01 SSH
    1. Install the git on EC2.

    2. Run the below command to generate the SSH Key
        ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "your_email@example.com"

    3. Start SSH agent & add key
        eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
        ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

    4. Copy your public key
        cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

    5. Add key to your Git provider
        On GitHub → Settings → SSH and GPG keys or add the key using deploy keys feature.
        
    6. Test connection
        ssh -T git@github.com

    7. Clone your repo
        git clone git@github.com:username/repo.git

    8. To clone specific branch
        git clone -b BRANCH_NAME --single-branch git@github.com:USERNAME/REPO.git




Option: 02 HTTPS + Personal Access Token (PAT)
1. Generate a token
    Create a token from:
    GitHub → Developer settings → Personal access tokens

2. Clone using HTTPS
    git clone https://github.com/username/repo.git
    When prompted:

    Username → your username
    Password → paste the token (not your actual password)

    Optional: Store credentials
    git config --global credential.helper store